# docs/

Documentation for the entire LP Internal AI system. Organized into setup guides, connector specs, runbooks, user guides, and architecture references.

## Subfolders

### setup/ — Infrastructure Setup Guides (14 guides)
Step-by-step setup for each phase of the AWS stack, numbered 00–23:
- `00-bootstrap.md` — monorepo, git, pnpm
- `01-aws-baseline.md` — AWS account + IAM
- `02-rds-postgres.md` — RDS Postgres + pgvector
- `03-secrets-manager.md` — AWS Secrets Manager
- `04-prisma-schema.md` — 30-model schema design
- `05-google-connectors.md` — Sheets + Drive syncs
- `06-embeddings-pgvector.md` — OpenAI embeddings + vector search
- `07-mcp-server.md` — MCP stdio + HTTP transport
- `08-hq-dashboard.md` — Next.js + NextAuth
- `09-ecs-express-mode.md` — ECS Fargate deployment
- `10-eventbridge-cron.md` — Scheduled syncs
- `11-sentry.md` — Error monitoring
- `12-notion.md` — Notion connector
- `README.md` — index with ✅/🟡/🔲 status per phase

### data-sources/ — Connector Architecture (5 guides)
One spec per connector: schema, auth method, tables written, error handling.
- `google-sheets-connector.md`, `google-drive-connector.md`, `notion-connector.md`, `aplos-connector.md`, `slack-connector.md`

### runbooks/ — Operational Procedures (3 guides)
- `local-dev.md` — Docker Compose + `.env` setup for local development
- `credentials-checklist.md` — Every API key: what it unlocks and how to get it
- `aws-permissions.md` — IAM policy matrix for developer/deployer/service roles

### user-guides/ — End-User & Developer Docs (2 guides)
- `using-the-mcp-server.md` — Connecting via Claude.ai, Desktop, or Code; tool discovery; rate limits; example queries
- `developing-tools-and-hq.md` — Adding new MCP tools; Prisma query patterns; testing

### Root-level Architecture Docs
- `database-schema.md` — All 30 Postgres tables with columns, indexes, and foreign keys
- `entity-resolution.md` — How students/staff are matched across sources (exact → fuzzy → pending)
- `mcp-server-spec.md` — All 16 tool definitions with input/output schemas and rate limits

### reference/v0-migrations/ — Legacy SQL
Pre-Prisma migration files kept for historical reference.
